#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""delegation-ledger: record delegated agents, and list the ones that never finished.

  delegation-ledger hook            SubagentStart/SubagentStop/PostToolUse hook body (stdin:
                                    hook JSON)
  delegation-ledger open [--hours N]
                                    agents whose latest event is not a stop, with evidence;
                                    thresholds in skills/delegation/liveness.toml
  delegation-ledger watch [--summary]
                                    one line per live delegation, Claude and Codex; --summary
                                    prints a token like `2▶ 1⚠` for the tmux status bar
  delegation-ledger tail [-n N]     the last N rows (including policy and spawn-guard denials,
                                    deadline nudges and exclusions)
  delegation-ledger audit [--hours N] [--monthly]
                                    is enforcement still binding? policy heartbeat, writers that
                                    changed the main checkout, rejected reports, denials;
                                    --monthly covers 30 days and adds the usage sections for
                                    retuning liveness.toml and [deadline]
  delegation-ledger exclude [--id ID] [--session SID] [--name NAME] --why TEXT
                                    leave matching rows (a probe, say) out of --monthly's usage
                                    sections; appends an `exclude` row
  delegation-ledger sandbox-denials [--days N]
                                    hosts and paths the sandbox refused, from the transcripts
  delegation-ledger canary [--quick] [--accept-fewer]
                                    re-verify enforcement on this Claude Code version: the quick
                                    tier (unit tests, sandbox posture, strings in the binary),
                                    then the live harness; records the result for `due`
  delegation-ledger due [--hook]    what is due (canary, audit, the monthly audit, dated items in
                                    due.toml); --hook is the SessionStart body, which also starts
                                    the cheap checks
  delegation-ledger wait [--pid N]... [--file PATH] [--log PATH [--done RE] [--fail RE]
                         [--stale MIN]] [--codex RUN_ID] [--desc TEXT] [--max MIN]
  delegation-ledger wait --resume ID [--max MIN] | --drop ID
                                    wait on a long job as a recorded watch, and exit before the
                                    Bash tool's 2-hour cap with the re-arm command. Launch it
                                    bare, with run_in_background and timeout 7200000. Exits:
                                    0 done; 1 the job failed; 2 the log went stale; 3 this
                                    waiter stepped aside (taken over, dropped, or its file is
                                    gone); 64 bad usage; 70 internal error; 75 still running at
                                    --max (110 min by default)

The hook always exits 0, so a ledger bug can never block an agent (failing open is correct
here, unlike the spawn guard). Its own errors go to
$XDG_STATE_HOME/dotclaude/delegation-ledger.err. Besides the ledger row, it keeps
agents/<id>.json, the per-agent liveness index: the agent's state, when its current activation
started, how many activations it has had, and its transcript path.

It prints nothing, except for the deadline nudge on PostToolUse. Past the role's nudge_min
(policy.toml [deadline]), an agent's next successful call gets one additionalContext reminder
per activation, recorded as `nudged` in its index and as a `nudge` row. subagent-policy
enforces the stop that follows.

For an agent in a worktree, the start and stop rows also carry a hash of the main checkout's
`git status` (main_before, main_after). The sandbox lets a worktree agent's subprocess write
anywhere in the session repo, so a computed-path write into the main checkout can't be
stopped, only seen. `audit` reports a changed hash as evidence, not a verdict, because the
lead may have been editing too.

`open` only suggests. Each row prints the evidence it used (parent session alive, how long
this activation has run, the newest transcript entry and its age, the calls still open), so
a verdict can be checked, never just trusted. The session rule follows cctop's
(github.com/stefanprodan/cctop, Apache-2.0), reimplemented: ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json maps
a session to a live pid. The rest comes from the agent transcript, not from per-call hooks. A
tool_use is written before the tool runs, a denied, failed or interrupted call still gets a
tool_result (but no PostToolUse), and every entry carries a timestamp. So a tool_use with no
tool_result is a call in flight, and its timestamp says since when. A session file's
procStart must match the pid's start time too, so a reused pid doesn't read as alive.

`watch` uses `open`'s rule for what is unfinished, but lists only what is live: an orphan or a
dead Codex run gets one footer line that points at `open`, and the tmux token never counts
it. It reads only the ledger's last 1 MiB, so a 3-second poll stays cheap as the ledger grows.

Inside the Bash sandbox no session pid is visible: each sandboxed command gets its own PID
namespace. Both views detect that (dc.pids_visible: SANDBOX_RUNTIME=1, or a CLAUDE_PID that
isn't alive with no live Claude process among the caller's parents), print a warning first, and
call a session unknown instead of gone. delegation-ledger is in sandbox.excludedCommands, so a
bare call runs outside the sandbox and is exact; a piped one stays inside and warns.

`wait` exists because Claude Code stops a background command at its timeout (2 hours at most)
and its wake-up note then says not to restart it. The waiter records a watch
(watches/<id>.json; delegation_common documents its fields, which the watch guard reads), polls
every 15 s and refreshes the watch's heartbeat each time. Every condition given must hold for
done, and the pids all exiting with another part unmet is failed. A --pid must be watchable
when the wait starts: running, this user's, and not pid 1 or a kernel thread (a pid echoed from
a sandboxed command can name any of those out here), and its command name is recorded. A log line is matched once complete (a last line without a newline, once the
job is over). --codex stands alone: once Codex and its wrapper are gone, the waiter runs the
`codex-delegate` beside this script as `finalize <run_id>` unless the run has a stop row, and
the stop row's exit decides. No option or variable runs a command of the caller's, since the
waiter runs outside the sandbox and one would be a sandbox escape. Inside the sandbox it can't
see the job, so it refuses there before writing anything. At --max it prints one line, `still
running: re-arm with delegation-ledger wait --resume <id> (run_in_background, timeout
7200000)`, and exits 75 with the watch still open. --resume takes the watch over and clears
blocked_at; --drop marks it dropped. A waiter whose watch was taken over, dropped or deleted
steps aside at its next poll. Its exit codes:
  0 done; 1 the job failed; 2 the log went stale; 3 this waiter stepped aside; 64 bad usage;
  70 internal error, or nothing could be decided (a codex finalize recorded no stop row, or the
  run left the ledger), with the watch left open for a --resume and the details in
  delegation-ledger.err; 75 still running at --max (at most 110 minutes, leaving the 5-minute
  finalize room under the cap). A codex run gets one unresolved watch, whatever the session,
  and a --resume moves the watch to the resuming session.
While it finalizes a codex run the waiter keeps its heartbeat, and it marks the watch as
finalizing, so a waiter that takes over meanwhile waits for that stop row instead of writing
a second one.
`watch` and `open` list unresolved watches in a block of their own, printed only when there
are some. Each wait start prunes ended watches over 7 days old.
"""
import argparse
import collections
import datetime
import glob
import hashlib
import json
import math
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import tomllib
import traceback

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import delegation_common as dc  # noqa: E402


def checks():
    # Imported on use, so the hook path never depends on the check code.
    import delegation_checks
    return delegation_checks


def handback_message(path):
    """The report a subagent delivered through the SubagentHandback tool, which is how
    reports arrive in auto mode. Then the SubagentStop input's last_assistant_message is
    empty (code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks: "The report is that call's `message` input")."""
    try:
        with open(os.path.expanduser(path), "rb") as f:
            f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            f.seek(max(0, f.tell() - 1048576))
            lines = f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines()
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return ""
    handbacks, failed = [], set()  # report-check may have sent earlier ones back
    for line in lines:
        try:
            e = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        for c in (e.get("message") or {}).get("content") or []:
            if not isinstance(c, dict):
                continue
            if c.get("type") == "tool_use" and c.get("name") == "SubagentHandback":
                handbacks.append((c.get("id"), (c.get("input") or {}).get("message") or ""))
            elif c.get("type") == "tool_result" and c.get("is_error"):
                failed.add(c.get("tool_use_id"))
    accepted = [m for i, m in handbacks if i not in failed]
    return (accepted or [m for _, m in handbacks] or [""])[-1]


def main_status(cwd):
    """sha256 of the main checkout's `git status` for an agent in a worktree, else None."""
    if not cwd or "/.claude/worktrees/" not in cwd:
        return None
    main = cwd.split("/.claude/worktrees/", 1)[0]  # the outermost, as subagent-policy protects
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", main, "status", "--porcelain=v1", "-uall"],
                             capture_output=True, timeout=3).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return "unknown"
    return hashlib.sha256(out).hexdigest()[:16]


def cmd_hook(_args):
    try:
        data = json.loads(sys.stdin.read() or "{}")
        event = data.get("hook_event_name")
        if event == "PostToolUse":
            nudge(data, time.time())
            return 0
        if event not in ("SubagentStart", "SubagentStop"):
            raise ValueError(f"unexpected hook_event_name {event!r}")
        meta = dc.agent_meta(data)
        base = {
            "ts": dc.now_iso(),
            "runner": "claude",
            "id": dc.norm_id(data.get("agent_id")),
            "agent_type": dc.agent_role(data, meta),
            "session_id": data.get("session_id"),
        }
        if meta.get("name"):
            base["name"] = meta["name"]  # agent_type is the role; for a teammate this its name
        if meta.get("teamName"):
            # Its stops fire per message, so a stop row's report_ok isn't a report's verdict.
            base["teammate"] = True
        if not base["id"]:
            raise ValueError(f"{event}: no agent_id in hook input")
        if not base["agent_type"]:
            # Claude Code's own helper agents fire SubagentStop with an empty agent_type and
            # leave no transcript. They are not delegations, so they stay out of the ledger.
            return 0
        if event == "SubagentStart":
            row = dict(base, event="start", cwd=data.get("cwd"),
                       parent_transcript=data.get("transcript_path"))
            mb = main_status(data.get("cwd"))
            if mb:
                row["main_before"] = mb
        else:
            text, source = data.get("last_assistant_message") or "", "last_message"
            if not text.strip():
                text = handback_message(data.get("agent_transcript_path"))
                source = "handback" if text.strip() else None
            ok, status, err = dc.report_check(text)
            row = dict(base, event="stop", agent_transcript=data.get("agent_transcript_path"),
                       report_ok=ok, report_status=status, report_error=err,
                       report_source=source)
            ma = main_status(data.get("cwd"))
            if ma:
                row["main_after"] = ma
        dc.append_row(row)
        index_agent(event, base, data)
    except Exception:
        try:
            os.makedirs(dc.state_dir(), exist_ok=True)
            with open(os.path.join(dc.state_dir(), "delegation-ledger.err"), "a") as f:
                f.write(f"{dc.now_iso()} {traceback.format_exc(limit=3)}\n")
        except Exception:
            pass
    return 0


def index_agent(event, base, data):
    """Keep agents/<id>.json, the liveness index `open`, `watch` and the deadline read."""
    if event == "SubagentStart":
        transcript = agent_transcript({"id": base["id"],
                                       "parent_transcript": data.get("transcript_path")})

        def start(s):
            # A SendMessage resume or a teammate's next message is a new activation of the
            # same agent: a fresh activation_start and budget (so no `nudged` yet), the same
            # first_start.
            s.update(id=base["id"], agent_type=base["agent_type"], name=base.get("name"),
                     teammate=bool(base.get("teammate")), session_id=base["session_id"],
                     agent_transcript=transcript, cwd=data.get("cwd"), state="running",
                     activation_start=base["ts"], activations=s.get("activations", 0) + 1)
            s.setdefault("first_start", base["ts"])
            s.pop("stopped_at", None)
            s.pop("nudged", None)
        dc.update_agent_state(base["id"], start)
        dc.prune_agent_states()
    else:
        dc.update_agent_state(base["id"], lambda s: s.update(
            id=base["id"], state="stopped", stopped_at=base["ts"]))


NUDGE = ("[deadline] This activation has run {ran} min, past the {nudge} min nudge for {role}. "
         "Report now: finish and hand back, or hand back `partial` naming what is left. At the "
         "{stop} min stop, every tool except {allow} is denied.")


def load_deadline():
    """policy.toml, or None when its [deadline] is unreadable or malformed. The nudge fails
    open on that, as report-check does, while subagent-policy fails closed on the same file."""
    try:
        with open(dc.policy_path(), "rb") as f:
            policy = tomllib.load(f)
        dc.check_deadline(policy.get("deadline"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):  # a TOMLDecodeError is a ValueError
        return None
    return policy


def nudge(data, now):
    """The PostToolUse body: once per activation, past the role's nudge_min, remind the agent
    to report. PostToolUse fires only for a call that succeeded, so the nudge rides the next
    successful call. Silent everywhere else."""
    aid = dc.norm_id(data.get("agent_id"))
    if not aid or not data.get("agent_type"):
        return  # the main thread, or one of Claude Code's helper agents
    idx = dc.read_agent_state(aid)
    if not idx or idx.get("nudged"):
        return  # no index means no clock; checked here so a nudged agent never takes the lock
    age = dc.activation_age(idx, now)
    policy = load_deadline() if age is not None else None
    if policy is None:
        return
    role = dc.agent_role(data, dc.agent_meta(data))
    nudge_s, stop_s = dc.deadline_for(policy, role)
    if age < nudge_s:
        return
    won = False

    def mark(s):
        # Parallel calls race here, so only the first under the lock, in the same activation,
        # sets the flag and prints.
        nonlocal won
        if not s.get("nudged") and s.get("activation_start") == idx["activation_start"]:
            s["nudged"] = dc.now_iso()
            won = True
    dc.update_agent_state(aid, mark)
    if not won:
        return
    print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {
        "hookEventName": "PostToolUse",
        "additionalContext": NUDGE.format(
            ran=dc.minutes_text(age), nudge=dc.minutes_text(nudge_s), role=role,
            stop=dc.minutes_text(stop_s), allow=dc.tool_list(policy["deadline"]["allow"])),
    }}))
    dc.append_row({"ts": dc.now_iso(), "runner": "claude", "event": "nudge", "id": aid,
                   "agent_type": role, "session_id": data.get("session_id"),
                   "minutes": round(age / 60, 1)})


def agent_transcript(entry):
    if entry.get("agent_transcript"):
        return os.path.expanduser(entry["agent_transcript"])
    parent = entry.get("parent_transcript")
    if not parent:
        return None
    parent = os.path.expanduser(parent)
    return os.path.join(parent[:-len(".jsonl")] if parent.endswith(".jsonl") else parent,
                        "subagents", f"agent-{entry['id']}.jsonl")


def entry_ts(e):
    """A transcript entry's timestamp in epoch seconds, or None. Transcript timestamps carry
    milliseconds, which dc.parse_iso doesn't take."""
    try:
        return datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(e["timestamp"].replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp()
    except (KeyError, AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def entry_kind(e, msg, kinds):
    if e.get("type") == "user":
        return "tool_result" if "tool_result" in kinds else "prompt"
    if "tool_use" in kinds:
        return "tool_use"
    if msg.get("stop_reason"):
        return f"turn ended ({msg['stop_reason']})"
    return "thinking" if "thinking" in kinds else "text"


def records(lines):
    """(ts, kind, blocks) for each user and assistant entry in transcript lines; ts may be
    None. Claude Code's attachment entries are skipped, and so is a line that doesn't parse (a
    window may cut the first one)."""
    for line in lines:
        try:
            e = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if not isinstance(e, dict) or e.get("type") not in ("user", "assistant"):
            continue
        msg = e.get("message") if isinstance(e.get("message"), dict) else {}
        content = msg.get("content")
        blocks = [c for c in content if isinstance(c, dict)] if isinstance(content, list) else []
        yield entry_ts(e), entry_kind(e, msg, {c.get("type") for c in blocks}), blocks


def scan_transcript(path):
    """What an agent transcript says about liveness, from its last 1 MiB (the bound
    handback_message uses). Returns a dict:
      open     [(tool, ts)], oldest first: the tool_use ids with no tool_result yet;
      last     the newest entry's kind: tool_use, tool_result, thinking, text, prompt or
               "turn ended (<stop_reason>)"; "no transcript" or "unreadable" when there is
               nothing to read;
      last_ts  the newest entry's time in epoch seconds, or None.
    Only user and assistant entries count, not Claude Code's attachment entries."""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            f.seek(max(0, f.tell() - 1048576))
            lines = f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines()
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return {"open": [], "last": "no transcript", "last_ts": None}
    uses, done = {}, set()
    last, last_ts = "unreadable", None
    for ts, kind, blocks in records(lines):
        if kind == "prompt":
            # A new prompt (a SendMessage resume, a teammate's next message) starts a new
            # turn, so a call an abort left without a tool_result is not in flight any more.
            uses.clear()
        for c in blocks:
            if c.get("type") == "tool_use":
                uses[c.get("id")] = (c.get("name") or "?", ts)
            elif c.get("type") == "tool_result":
                done.add(c.get("tool_use_id"))
        last, last_ts = kind, ts or last_ts
    calls = sorted((v for k, v in uses.items() if k not in done), key=lambda v: v[1] or 0)
    return {"open": calls, "last": last, "last_ts": last_ts}


LIVENESS_PATH = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(dc.HERE), "liveness.toml")
LIVENESS_DEFAULTS = {  # minutes; liveness.toml says why these values
    "subagent": {"silent_min": 15, "tool_min": 30},
    "teammate": {"silent_min": 30, "tool_min": 30},
    "codex": {"silent_min": 30},
}


def load_liveness():
    """(thresholds, warning) from $DELEGATION_LIVENESS, else skills/delegation/liveness.toml.
    It fails open, like due.toml: a missing or malformed file leaves all the defaults above,
    and a value that isn't a positive number leaves its own default. The warning says which,
    and `open` and `watch` print it first (`watch --summary` doesn't), so a broken file can't
    make them go quiet."""
    path = os.environ.get("DELEGATION_LIVENESS") or LIVENESS_PATH
    limits = {kind: dict(v) for kind, v in LIVENESS_DEFAULTS.items()}
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            data = tomllib.load(f)
    except (OSError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as ex:
        return limits, f"{path}: {ex}; using the default thresholds"
    problems = []
    for kind, table in data.items():
        if kind not in limits or not isinstance(table, dict):
            problems.append(f"[{kind}] is not one of {', '.join(limits)}")
            continue
        for key, val in table.items():
            if key not in limits[kind]:
                problems.append(f"{kind}.{key} is not a threshold")
            elif not dc.is_positive(val):
                problems.append(f"{kind}.{key} = {val!r} is not a positive number")
            else:
                limits[kind][key] = val
    return limits, (f"{path}: {'; '.join(problems)}; the defaults stand for those"
                    if problems else None)


def description(path):
    meta = path[:-len(".jsonl")] + ".meta.json" if path and path.endswith(".jsonl") else None
    try:
        with open(meta) as f:
            return (json.load(f).get("description") or "")[:60]
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return ""


def minutes(since, now):
    return (now - since) / 60


STOP_GRACE_MIN = 1  # an end_turn entry precedes its stop row by up to ~3 s (a worktree
                    # agent's `git status`), so a 3-second poll mustn't flag that gap


def claude_state(e, alive, limits, now):
    """What the transcript scan and the index say about a Claude ledger entry. `alive` is
    whether its session runs: True, False, or None when no pid is visible. Returns a dict:
      verdict   `open`'s text;
      short     `watch`'s text;
      warn      past tool_min or silent_min, or a turn that ended past the grace with no
                stop row;
      live      `alive`: False only when the session is known to be gone;
      evidence  what the verdict rests on;
      path      the agent transcript.
    A pending permission prompt shows as an open call."""
    idx = dc.read_agent_state(e["id"])
    path = agent_transcript(e) or idx.get("agent_transcript")
    lim = limits["teammate" if idx.get("teammate") or e.get("teammate") else "subagent"]
    try:
        began = dc.parse_iso(idx.get("activation_start") or e["ts"]).timestamp()
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
        began = now
    scan = scan_transcript(path)
    calls = scan["open"]
    warn = False
    if alive is False:
        verdict = "orphaned: its session is gone; redo it or resume from its artifact"
        short = "orphaned"
    elif calls:
        tool, t0 = calls[0]
        mins = minutes(t0 or began, now)
        verdict = short = f"in {tool} {int(mins)} min" + (f", +{len(calls) - 1} more"
                                                         if len(calls) > 1 else "")
        if mins >= lim["tool_min"]:
            warn = True
            verdict += f"  ⚠ past {lim['tool_min']:g} min: a long call or stuck; check it"
    elif scan["last"].startswith("turn ended"):
        # Without a timestamp the end can't be timed, so the grace doesn't apply.
        if scan["last_ts"] and minutes(scan["last_ts"], now) < STOP_GRACE_MIN:
            verdict = short = "finishing its turn"
        else:
            warn = True
            short = "ended its turn but no stop row"
            verdict = short + ": read its transcript for the report"
    else:
        quiet = minutes(scan["last_ts"] or began, now)
        warn = quiet >= lim["silent_min"]
        short = (f"no transcript entry for {int(quiet)} min" if warn else
                 f"running (no transcript entry for {int(quiet)} min)")
        verdict = short + ("  ⚠ ask it for status" if warn else "")
    k = idx.get("activations")
    session = ("unknown (no pid visible in the sandbox)" if alive is None else
               "alive" if alive else "gone")
    ev = (f"session {session}, active {int(minutes(began, now))} min"
          + (f" (activation {k})" if k else "")
          + f", last entry {scan['last']}"
          + (f" {int(minutes(scan['last_ts'], now))} min ago" if scan["last_ts"] else "")
          + (f", {len(calls)} call{'s' if len(calls) > 1 else ''} open" if calls else ""))
    return {"verdict": verdict, "short": short, "warn": warn, "live": alive,
            "evidence": ev, "path": path}


def codex_age(e, now):
    """Minutes since a codex run's events.jsonl last changed, or None."""
    try:
        return minutes(os.path.getmtime(os.path.join(e.get("out") or "", "events.jsonl")), now)
    except OSError:
        return None


def codex_entry(e, visible, limits, now):
    """claude_state's dict for a codex ledger entry. It is live while the codex pid runs, or
    while a pending row's wrapper does; None when no pid is visible."""
    verdict, ev = dc.codex_state(e, visible)
    age, cap = codex_age(e, now), limits["codex"]["silent_min"]
    warn = age is not None and age >= cap
    if warn:
        verdict += f"  ⚠ no event past {cap:g} min: check it"
    live = dc.codex_live(e) if visible else None
    last = f"last event {int(age)} min ago" if age is not None else "no events yet"
    if e.get("event") == "pending" and live:
        short = "starting"
    else:
        short = f"{'pid not visible' if live is None else 'running'}, {last}"
    return {"verdict": verdict, "short": short, "warn": warn, "live": live,
            "evidence": ev, "path": e.get("out")}


def unfinished(rows, horizon):
    """[(runner, id, entry)], oldest first: the folded entries whose latest event isn't a
    stop, from `horizon` (epoch seconds) on. `open` and `watch` share this rule, so the two
    views can't disagree about what is unfinished."""
    out = []
    for (runner, rid), e in sorted(dc.fold(rows).items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1].get("ts", "")):
        if e.get("event") == "stop":
            continue
        try:
            if dc.parse_iso(e["ts"]).timestamp() < horizon:
                continue
        except (KeyError, ValueError):
            continue
        out.append((runner, rid, e))
    return out


SANDBOX_WARNING = ("no pid is visible inside the Bash sandbox, so a gone session looks like a "
                   "live one; run delegation-ledger as a bare command (it is in "
                   "excludedCommands)")


def liveness_context():
    """(limits, warnings, visible, sessions), computed once per view. `sessions` is None when
    no pid is visible, which makes every Claude entry's `alive` None."""
    limits, warning = load_liveness()
    visible = dc.pids_visible()
    warnings = ([] if visible else [SANDBOX_WARNING]) + ([warning] if warning else [])
    return limits, warnings, visible, (dc.live_sessions() if visible else None)


def state_of(runner, e, ctx, now):
    limits, _, visible, sessions = ctx
    if runner == "codex":
        return codex_entry(e, visible, limits, now)
    alive = None if sessions is None else e.get("session_id") in sessions
    return claude_state(e, alive, limits, now)


def cmd_open(args):
    now = time.time()
    ctx = liveness_context()
    for w in ctx[1]:
        print(f"warning: {w}")
    entries = unfinished(dc.read_rows(), now - args.hours * 3600)
    for runner, rid, e in entries:
        s = state_of(runner, e, ctx, now)
        if runner == "codex":
            print(f"codex  {rid}  {e.get('event')}  {s['verdict']}\n"
                  f"       {s['evidence']}; out {e.get('out')}")
        else:
            print(f"claude {rid}  {e.get('agent_type')}  {description(s['path'])!r}  "
                  f"{s['verdict']}\n       {s['evidence']}")
    if not entries:
        print(f"no unfinished delegations in the last {args.hours:g}h")
    for line in watch_block(ctx, now, now - args.hours * 3600, detail=True):
        print(line)
    return 0


def last_seen(w):
    """A watch's last heartbeat, else its creation, in epoch seconds; 0 when neither parses."""
    try:
        return dc.parse_iso(w.get("waiter_heartbeat") or w["created"]).timestamp()
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return 0


def watch_block(ctx, now, horizon, detail):
    """The unresolved watches seen since `horizon`, and those that ended while no Claude process
    was listening and aren't reported yet (dc.ended_unheard, where pids are visible), as lines
    under a `watches:` header: one each for `watch`, two with the evidence for `open`
    (`detail`). [] when there are none, so neither view's output changes."""
    _, _, visible, sessions = ctx
    lines = []
    for w in dc.all_watches():
        if last_seen(w) < horizon:
            continue
        wid, desc = w.get("id"), (w.get("description") or "")[:40]
        cond = dc.condition_text(w.get("condition") or {})
        if w.get("state") not in dc.UNRESOLVED:
            if visible and dc.ended_unheard(w, now):
                news = (f"ended {w.get('state')} while no Claude Code process was listening ⚠ "
                        "check the result")
                lines += ([f"  {wid}  {desc!r}  {news}"] if not detail else
                          [f"  {wid}  {w.get('state')}  {desc!r}  waited for {cond}",
                           f"         {news} (ended {w.get('ended')}, session "
                           f"{w.get('session_id')})"])
            continue
        rearm = f"re-arm: delegation-ledger wait --resume {wid}"
        alive = dc.waiter_alive(w, now) if visible else None
        ack = "  (acknowledged)" if w.get("state") == "acknowledged" else ""
        if not detail:
            status = ("waiter not visible in the sandbox" if alive is None else
                      "waiter alive" if alive else f"no live waiter ⚠ {rearm}")
            # A --desc hides the condition, so it's shown too: a wrong pid's name stands out.
            what = "" if w.get("description") == cond else f"  {cond}"
            lines.append(f"  {wid}  {desc!r}{what}  {status}{ack}")
            continue
        session = ("unknown" if sessions is None else
                   "alive" if w.get("session_id") in sessions else "gone")
        if alive is None:
            waiter = f"waiter pid {w.get('waiter_pid')} not visible in the sandbox"
        else:
            running = dc.pid_alive(w.get("waiter_pid"), w.get("waiter_start"))
            waiter = f"waiter pid {w.get('waiter_pid')} {'running' if running else 'gone'}"
        try:
            beat = (f"heartbeat {int(minutes(dc.parse_iso(w['waiter_heartbeat']).timestamp(), now))}"
                    " min ago")
        except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
            beat = "no heartbeat"
        lines.append(f"  {wid}  {w.get('state')}  {desc!r}  waiting for {cond}")
        lines.append(f"         session {w.get('session_id')} {session}, {waiter}, {beat}"
                     + ("" if alive else f"; {rearm}"))
    return ["watches:"] + lines if lines else []


WATCH_HOURS = 48
WATCH_TAIL = 1 << 20  # watch reads the ledger's last 1 MiB, so a 3-second poll stays cheap


def repo_name(path):
    """The repo a delegation works in: the basename of its directory, taken before any
    /.claude/worktrees/ so a worktree agent shows its repo."""
    return os.path.basename((path or "").split("/.claude/worktrees/", 1)[0].rstrip("/")) or "?"


def cmd_watch(args):
    now = time.time()
    ctx = liveness_context()
    lines, warned, gone = [], 0, 0
    for runner, rid, e in unfinished(dc.read_rows(tail=WATCH_TAIL), now - WATCH_HOURS * 3600):
        s = state_of(runner, e, ctx, now)
        if s["live"] is False:
            gone += 1  # orphans and dead codex runs: `open` has them, the bar never counts them
            continue
        warned += s["warn"]
        flag = " ⚠" if s["warn"] else ""
        if runner == "codex":
            lines.append(f"codex   {e.get('run_id') or rid}  {e.get('model')}  "
                         f"{repo_name(e.get('dir'))}  {s['short']}{flag}")
        else:
            desc = description(s["path"])[:40]
            lines.append(f"claude  {rid}  {e.get('agent_type')}  {repo_name(e.get('cwd'))}  "
                         f"{s['short']}{flag}" + (f"  {desc!r}" if desc else ""))
    if args.summary:
        print((f"{len(lines)}▶" + (f" {warned}⚠" if warned else "")) if lines else "")
        return 0
    for w in ctx[1]:
        print(f"warning: {w}")
    print("\n".join(lines) if lines else "no live delegations")
    if gone:
        print(f"{gone} more unfinished but not live in the last {WATCH_HOURS}h: "
              "delegation-ledger open")
    for line in watch_block(ctx, now, now - WATCH_HOURS * 3600, detail=False):
        print(line)
    return 0


def used_tools(path):
    try:
        with open(path, errors="replace") as f:
            return '"type":"tool_use"' in f.read().replace(" ", "")
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return False


def read_policy():
    """policy.toml as a dict, or {} when it can't be read. The audits only report, so they fail
    open on it, unlike subagent-policy."""
    try:
        with open(dc.policy_path(), "rb") as f:
            return tomllib.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):  # a TOMLDecodeError is a ValueError
        return {}


def report_roles(policy):
    table = policy.get("roles")
    roles = table.get("report_checked") if isinstance(table, dict) else None
    return set(roles) if isinstance(roles, list) else {"Explore", "researcher", "reviewer",
                                                       "writer"}


def cmd_audit(args):
    """Is enforcement still binding? Prints findings; exits 1 if any warning. --monthly widens
    the window to a month and adds the usage sections (see `usage`)."""
    hours = args.hours if args.hours is not None else (dc.MONTH_DAYS * 24 if args.monthly
                                                       else 168)
    horizon = time.time() - hours * 3600
    every = dc.read_rows()
    rows = [r for r in every if r.get("ts") and dc.parse_iso(r["ts"]).timestamp() >= horizon]
    warn = 0
    lines = []

    def say(line):  # each line also goes into the stamp `due` reads
        lines.append(line)
        print(line)

    hb = os.path.join(dc.state_dir(), "subagent-policy.heartbeat")
    hb_t = os.path.getmtime(hb) if os.path.exists(hb) else None
    # The policy hook updates the heartbeat on every delegated tool call. An agent that used
    # tools and stopped well after the last heartbeat means the hook never saw it: unwired,
    # or `agent_id` renamed in hook input by an upgrade.
    unseen = [r for r in rows if r.get("runner") == "claude" and r.get("event") == "stop"
              and (hb_t is None or dc.parse_iso(r["ts"]).timestamp() > hb_t + 120)
              and used_tools(r.get("agent_transcript"))]
    if unseen:
        warn += 1
        say(f"WARN policy hook: {len(unseen)} agent(s) used tools after its last heartbeat "
            f"({'never' if hb_t is None else time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M', time.localtime(hb_t))})."
            " Check the PreToolUse entry and that hook input still carries agent_id.")
    else:
        say("ok   policy hook: saw every agent that used tools")
    # Fold the whole ledger, then keep the agents whose latest row is in the window: a writer
    # that started before the window and stopped inside it still pairs its start and stop.
    folded = {k: e for k, e in dc.fold(every).items()
              if e.get("ts") and dc.parse_iso(e["ts"]).timestamp() >= horizon}
    moved = [(k, e) for k, e in folded.items()
             if e.get("main_before") and e.get("main_after")
             and e["main_before"] != e["main_after"]]
    for (_, rid), e in moved:
        warn += 1
        say(f"WARN main checkout changed while {e.get('agent_type')} {rid} ran in its worktree "
            "(evidence, not proof: the lead may have edited too). Inspect `git status` there.")
    if not moved:
        say("ok   no worktree agent coincided with a main-checkout change")
    policy = read_policy()
    roles = report_roles(policy)
    bad = [e for e in folded.values() if e.get("event") == "stop" and e.get("report_ok") is False
           and e.get("agent_type") in roles and not e.get("teammate")]
    say(f"{'WARN' if bad else 'ok  '} reports failing the contract: {len(bad)}")
    warn += bool(bad)
    denials = collections.Counter((r.get("agent_type"), r.get("rule")) for r in rows
                                  if r.get("event") == "policy")
    say(f"info policy denials in the last {hours:g}h: {sum(denials.values())}")
    for (atype, rule), n in denials.most_common(10):
        say(f"       {n:3}  {atype}  {rule}")
    if args.monthly:
        warn += usage(every, horizon, hours, policy, say)
    try:
        checks().stamp_audit(hours, lines, shown=not args.unshown)
        if args.monthly and hours >= dc.MONTH_DAYS * 24:
            # A narrower run doesn't count, so it can't silence `due`'s monthly nudge.
            checks().update_state("audit.json", monthly=dc.now_iso())
    except OSError:
        pass  # the sandbox's read-only state dir: a manual audit there just isn't stamped
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001  the stamp is for `due`; the audit itself stands
        checks().log_error()
    return 1 if warn else 0


# The monthly audit: what delegation looked like over a month, the numbers for retuning
# liveness.toml and policy.toml [deadline]. It only shows them; picking new values stays a
# human call. These two thresholds only inform, so they live here, not in policy.toml, whose
# parse error would block every delegated call.
GP_WARN_SHARE = 0.25  # general-purpose agents get every tool and no report contract
MIN_SAMPLE = 20       # activations a group needs before its numbers are worth retuning on
SYNTHETIC = "hand-fed hook input"
UUID_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{8}(-[0-9a-f]{4}){3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$")
TEAMMATE_ID_RE = re.compile(r"^a.+-[0-9a-f]{16}$")  # a teammate's id embeds its name
EXCLUDE_KEYS = {"id": "id", "session": "session_id", "name": "name"}  # option -> row field
START_EVENTS = ("start", "resume")  # codex-delegate's resume starts a run too
SLACK = 1  # seconds: ledger stamps are whole seconds, transcript ones carry milliseconds

Activation = collections.namedtuple("Activation", "key role kind start end transcript")


def excluded(rows):
    """{row index: why} for the rows the usage sections leave out. A row matching every key of
    an `exclude` row takes its `why`. A claude row whose session_id isn't a UUID is hand-fed
    hook input (an install check run by hand, say), not a session. The exclude rows themselves
    aren't listed: nothing that reads lifecycle rows reads them."""
    rules = [({k: r[k] for k in EXCLUDE_KEYS.values() if r.get(k) is not None},
              r.get("why") or "excluded") for r in rows if r.get("event") == "exclude"]
    out = {}
    for i, r in enumerate(rows):
        if r.get("event") == "exclude":
            continue
        why = next((w for keys, w in rules
                    if keys and all(r.get(k) == v for k, v in keys.items())), None)
        if why is None and r.get("runner") == "claude" and not UUID_RE.match(
                str(r.get("session_id") or "")):
            why = SYNTHETIC
        if why:
            out[i] = why
    return out


def kind_of(row):
    if row.get("runner") == "codex":
        return "codex"
    return ("teammate" if row.get("teammate") or TEAMMATE_ID_RE.match(str(row.get("id") or ""))
            else "subagent")


def role_of(entry):
    """The role the audit counts a folded entry under. A teammate of a built-in type has no
    customAgentType, so its agent_type is its name (docs/delegation.md, A2's known gaps). It
    gets the default policy, as general-purpose does, so it counts as general-purpose."""
    atype = entry.get("agent_type")
    if kind_of(entry) == "teammate" and (atype == entry.get("name") or str(
            entry.get("id") or "").startswith(f"a{atype}-")):
        return "general-purpose"
    return atype


def row_ts(row):
    try:
        return dc.parse_iso(row["ts"]).timestamp()
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def activations(rows):
    """([Activation], unstarted, unstopped) from ledger rows in order. An activation runs from
    a start to the last stop before that agent's next start: an agent that ends with plain text
    in auto mode stops twice (P3 in docs/delegation.md). A codex run stops once, so its stop
    closes it. Agents with a stop but no start, or a
    start that no stop closed, come back as {key: ts}, counted but not timed. Claude Code's
    helper agents (an empty agent_type, logged before the ledger skipped them) are left out."""
    acts, cur, unstarted, unstopped = [], {}, {}, {}

    def close(key):
        a = cur.pop(key)
        if a["end"] is None:
            unstopped[key] = a["start"]
        else:
            acts.append(Activation(key, a["role"], a["kind"], a["start"], a["end"],
                                   a["transcript"]))

    for r in rows:
        event, key, t = r.get("event"), (r.get("runner"), r.get("id")), row_ts(r)
        role = "codex" if key[0] == "codex" else r.get("agent_type")
        if key[1] is None or t is None or not role or event not in START_EVENTS + ("stop",):
            continue
        if event != "stop":
            if key in cur:
                close(key)
            cur[key] = {"role": role, "kind": kind_of(r), "start": t, "end": None,
                        "transcript": agent_transcript(r)}
        elif key in cur:
            a = cur[key]
            # The stop row has the role meta.json resolved, and only it may say `teammate`.
            a.update(end=t, role=role, transcript=agent_transcript(r) or a["transcript"],
                     kind="teammate" if "teammate" in (a["kind"], kind_of(r)) else a["kind"])
            if key[0] == "codex":
                close(key)  # codex never stops twice: a later stop is a failed resume's
        else:
            unstarted[key] = t
    for key in list(cur):
        close(key)
    return acts, unstarted, unstopped


def transcript_gaps(path, t0, t1, cache=None):
    """(longest call, longest silence) in seconds, over the transcript entries inside one
    activation [t0, t1]; None when there are none to read. A call runs from its tool_use
    to its tool_result, to a new prompt (which ends an aborted call), or to t1. Silence is a
    gap between entries, from t0 up to t1, while no call is open: what liveness.toml's
    silent_min watches for. An activation with no entry in its window is unread too (a wrong
    path), not one long silence. `cache` keeps each file's timestamps and tool ids, not its
    content, since a teammate's activations share one transcript."""
    cache = {} if cache is None else cache
    if path not in cache:
        try:
            with open(path, "rb") as f:
                lines = f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines()
        except (OSError, TypeError):
            lines = None
        cache[path] = None if lines is None else [
            (ts, kind, [(c["type"], c.get("id") if c["type"] == "tool_use" else
                         c.get("tool_use_id")) for c in blocks
                        if c.get("type") in ("tool_use", "tool_result")])
            for ts, kind, blocks in records(lines) if ts is not None]
    entries = [e for e in cache[path] or () if t0 - SLACK <= e[0] <= t1 + SLACK]
    if not entries:
        return None
    calls, call, silence, prev = {}, 0.0, 0.0, t0
    for ts, kind, tools in entries:
        if not calls:
            silence = max(silence, ts - prev)
        if kind == "prompt":
            call = max([call] + [ts - s for s in calls.values()])
            calls.clear()
        for typ, cid in tools:
            if typ == "tool_use":
                calls[cid] = ts
            elif cid in calls:
                call = max(call, ts - calls.pop(cid))
        prev = ts
    call = max([call] + [t1 - s for s in calls.values()])
    if not calls:
        silence = max(silence, t1 - prev)
    return call, silence


def pct(values, p):
    """The nearest-rank percentile of a non-empty list."""
    s = sorted(values)
    return s[max(0, math.ceil(p * len(s)) - 1)]


def duration_table(acts, policy):
    """One row per subagent role, busiest first, then teammates and codex: the activation
    count, p50, p90 and max in minutes, the [deadline] budget (nudge/stop, or "per role" for
    teammates of mixed roles), and how many activations ran past each. With policy None (an
    unreadable [deadline]) or for codex, which keeps its own --timeout, the budget columns are
    None."""
    groups = collections.defaultdict(list)
    for a in acts:
        groups[a.role if a.kind == "subagent" else
               {"teammate": "teammates", "codex": "codex"}[a.kind]].append(a)
    out = []
    for label, group in sorted(groups.items(), key=lambda kv: (
            kv[0] in ("teammates", "codex"), kv[0] == "codex", -len(kv[1]), kv[0])):
        mins = [(a.end - a.start) / 60 for a in group]
        row = {"label": label, "n": len(mins), "p50": pct(mins, .5), "p90": pct(mins, .9),
               "max": max(mins), "few": len(mins) < MIN_SAMPLE, "budget": None,
               "past_nudge": None, "past_stop": None}
        if policy is not None and label != "codex":
            budgets = [dc.deadline_for(policy, a.role) for a in group]
            row["past_nudge"] = sum(m * 60 >= b[0] for m, b in zip(mins, budgets))
            row["past_stop"] = sum(m * 60 >= b[1] for m, b in zip(mins, budgets))
            row["budget"] = (f"{dc.minutes_text(budgets[0][0])}/{dc.minutes_text(budgets[0][1])}"
                             if len(set(budgets)) == 1 else "per role")
        out.append(row)
    return out


def silence_table(acts, limits, cache):
    """Per kind (subagent, teammate): the activations, how many had a readable transcript,
    and over those the p90 and max of the longest call and the longest silence in minutes,
    with how many crossed liveness.toml's tool_min and silent_min."""
    out = []
    for kind in ("subagent", "teammate"):
        group = [a for a in acts if a.kind == kind]
        if not group:
            continue
        gaps = [g for g in (transcript_gaps(a.transcript, a.start, a.end, cache) for a in group)
                if g is not None]
        row = {"kind": kind, "n": len(group), "read": len(gaps)}
        if gaps:
            calls, quiet, lim = [c / 60 for c, _ in gaps], [s / 60 for _, s in gaps], limits[kind]
            row.update(call_p90=pct(calls, .9), call_max=max(calls), tool_min=lim["tool_min"],
                       past_tool=sum(c >= lim["tool_min"] for c in calls),
                       quiet_p90=pct(quiet, .9), quiet_max=max(quiet),
                       silent_min=lim["silent_min"],
                       past_silent=sum(q >= lim["silent_min"] for q in quiet))
        out.append(row)
    return out


def usage(every, horizon, hours, policy, say):
    """The monthly audit's usage sections, over the window and without the excluded rows (the
    enforcement checks above read every row: a probe the policy hook missed is still a miss).
    Returns 1 when the general-purpose share warned, else 0."""
    skip = excluded(every)
    in_window = lambda r: (row_ts(r) or 0) >= horizon  # noqa: E731
    taken = {(w, every[i].get("runner"), every[i].get("id")) for i, w in skip.items()
             if in_window(every[i])}
    left = collections.Counter(w for w, _, _ in taken)  # distinct agents per reason
    rows = [r for i, r in enumerate(every) if i not in skip]
    agents = {k: e for k, e in dc.fold(rows).items()
              if in_window(e) and (k[0] == "codex" or e.get("agent_type"))}
    claude = [e for k, e in agents.items() if k[0] == "claude"]
    acts, unstarted, unstopped = activations(rows)
    acts = [a for a in acts if a.end >= horizon]
    silence = silence_table(acts, load_liveness()[0], {})

    say(f"info usage over the last {hours / 24:g} days, without the excluded rows")
    say(f"info coverage: {len(claude)} agents, {len(agents) - len(claude)} codex runs; left out: "
        + (", ".join(f"{w} {n}" for w, n in sorted(left.items())) or "none")
        + f"; transcripts read for {sum(r['read'] for r in silence)}/"
        f"{sum(r['n'] for r in silence)} activations")

    types = collections.Counter(role_of(e) for e in claude)
    say("info agents by type:")
    for atype, n in types.most_common():
        say(f"       {n:4}  {n / len(claude):4.0%}  {atype}")
    share = types.get("general-purpose", 0) / len(claude) if claude else 0
    warn = share > GP_WARN_SHARE
    say(f"{'WARN' if warn else 'ok  '} general-purpose share {share:.0%} (warns over "
        f"{GP_WARN_SHARE:.0%}): it gets every tool and no report contract; a teammate with no "
        "recorded role counts here")
    spawn = policy.get("spawn")
    prefix = spawn.get("team_prefix") if isinstance(spawn, dict) else None
    prefix = prefix if isinstance(prefix, str) and prefix else "team-"
    mates = sorted(e.get("name") or e.get("agent_type") for e in claude
                   if kind_of(e) == "teammate")
    say(f"info teammates: {len(mates)} ({sum(m.startswith(prefix) for m in mates)} with the "
        f"{prefix} prefix)" + (": " + ", ".join(mates) if mates else ""))
    spawns = collections.Counter(f"{r.get('name')} ({r.get('subagent_type')})" for r in rows
                                 if r.get("event") == "policy" and r.get("rule") == "named-spawn"
                                 and in_window(r))
    say(f"info named-spawn denials: {sum(spawns.values())}" + (": " + ", ".join(
        s + (f" x{n}" if n > 1 else "") for s, n in sorted(spawns.items())) if spawns else ""))

    say("info minutes per activation, against policy.toml [deadline] (nudge/stop):")
    say(f"       {'':18}{'n':>5}{'p50':>7}{'p90':>7}{'max':>7}{'budget':>9}{'>nudge':>8}"
        f"{'>stop':>7}")
    for r in duration_table(acts, load_deadline()):
        dash = lambda v: "-" if v is None else v  # noqa: E731
        say(f"       {r['label']:18}{r['n']:5}{r['p50']:7.1f}{r['p90']:7.1f}{r['max']:7.1f}"
            f"{dash(r['budget']):>9}{dash(r['past_nudge']):>8}{dash(r['past_stop']):>7}"
            + ("  too few to retune" if r["few"] else ""))
    unstarted = sum(t >= horizon for t in unstarted.values())
    unstopped = sum(t >= horizon for t in unstopped.values())
    if unstarted or unstopped:
        say(f"       not timed: {unstarted} agent(s) with a stop but no start, {unstopped} with a "
            "start that no stop closed")
    say("info longest call and longest silence per activation, minutes, against liveness.toml:")
    for r in silence:
        if not r["read"]:
            say(f"       {r['kind']:10} no readable transcript for its {r['n']} activations")
            continue
        say(f"       {r['kind']:10} {r['read']} read: call p90 {r['call_p90']:.1f} max "
            f"{r['call_max']:.1f}, {r['past_tool']} past tool_min {r['tool_min']:g}; silence "
            f"p90 {r['quiet_p90']:.1f} max {r['quiet_max']:.1f}, {r['past_silent']} past "
            f"silent_min {r['silent_min']:g}" + ("  too few to retune" if r["read"] < MIN_SAMPLE
                                                else ""))

    roles = report_roles(policy)
    stops = [e for e in claude if e.get("event") == "stop" and kind_of(e) != "teammate"
             and e.get("agent_type") in roles]
    rates = collections.defaultdict(lambda: [0, 0])
    for e in stops:
        rates[e["agent_type"]][0] += e.get("report_ok") is True
        rates[e["agent_type"]][1] += 1
    say("info reports passing the contract (each agent's last stop; teammates left out): "
        + (", ".join(f"{t} {ok}/{n}" for t, (ok, n) in sorted(rates.items())) or "none"))

    def per_role(event, rule=None):
        seen = {(r.get("agent_type"), r.get("id")) for r in rows if r.get("event") == event
                and (rule is None or r.get("rule") == rule) and in_window(r)}
        return ", ".join(f"{t} {n}" for t, n in sorted(
            collections.Counter(t for t, _ in seen).items())) or "none"
    say(f"info deadline: nudged {per_role('nudge')}; stopped {per_role('policy', 'deadline')} "
        "(distinct agents)")
    return int(warn)


def cmd_exclude(args):
    """Append an `exclude` row, so the monthly audit's usage sections leave the matching rows
    out. It refuses a key-less or unmatched exclusion, so a typo can't silently do nothing."""
    keys = {field: getattr(args, opt) for opt, field in EXCLUDE_KEYS.items()
            if getattr(args, opt) is not None}
    if "id" in keys:
        keys["id"] = dc.norm_id(keys["id"])  # the ledger keys agents without `agent-`
    if not keys:
        print("exclude: give --id, --session or --name", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    hits = [r for r in dc.read_rows() if r.get("event") != "exclude"
            and all(r.get(k) == v for k, v in keys.items())]
    if not hits:
        print(f"exclude: no ledger row matches {json.dumps(keys)}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        dc.append_row(dict(keys, ts=dc.now_iso(), event="exclude", why=args.why))
    except OSError as ex:
        print(f"exclude: can't write the ledger ({ex}); inside the Bash sandbox the state dir "
              "is read-only, so run it as a bare command", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(f"excluded {len(hits)} row(s) of {len({r.get('id') for r in hits})} agent(s) from "
          f"audit --monthly's usage sections: {args.why}")
    return 0


VIOLATION_RE = re.compile(r"deny (network-outbound|file-write|file-read)\S* ([^\s()\\\"]+)")


def cmd_sandbox_denials(args):
    """What the sandbox refused, from the transcripts: which hosts to allow, which paths hurt.
    Reads only the <sandbox_violations> lines Claude Code writes into tool results."""
    cutoff = time.time() - args.days * 86400
    seen = collections.Counter()
    for p in glob.glob(os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl")) + \
            glob.glob(os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/projects/*/*/subagents/*.jsonl")):
        try:
            if os.path.getmtime(p) < cutoff:
                continue
            with open(p, errors="replace") as f:
                text = f.read()
        except OSError:
            continue
        if "sandbox_violations" not in text:
            continue
        for kind, target in VIOLATION_RE.findall(text):
            seen[(kind, target)] += 1
    if not seen:
        print(f"no sandbox denials in the last {args.days:g} days")
    for (kind, target), n in seen.most_common():
        print(f"{n:4}  {kind:16}  {target}")
    return 0


def cmd_canary(args):
    return checks().canary(args.quick, accept_fewer=args.accept_fewer)


def cmd_due(args):
    if args.hook:
        return checks().hook_main(sys.stdin.read())
    if args.background is not None:
        return checks().background(args.background)
    return checks().status()


def cmd_tail(args):
    for r in dc.read_rows()[-args.n:]:
        print(json.dumps(r, sort_keys=True))
    return 0


WAIT_SANDBOXED = ("run delegation-ledger wait as a bare command (the sandbox hides other "
                  "processes)")
WAIT_LAUNCH = ("delegation-ledger: watch {0}. If this command is stopped, re-arm with "
               "delegation-ledger wait --resume {0} (run_in_background, timeout 7200000)")
WAIT_EXITS = {"done": 0, "failed": 1, "stale": 2}  # how the watch's condition ended
WAIT_ASIDE = 3    # this waiter stepped aside; the watch goes on, or was dropped
WAIT_USAGE = 64   # EX_USAGE
WAIT_ERROR = 70   # EX_SOFTWARE: nothing decided, the watch left open; see delegation-ledger.err
WAIT_AT_MAX = 75  # EX_TEMPFAIL: still running, so re-arm
WAIT_EXIT_HELP = """exit codes:
  0   done
  1   the job failed: a --fail match, its pids exited with another condition unmet, or the
      codex run stopped with a nonzero exit or never started
  2   the log went stale (--stale)
  3   this waiter stepped aside: a --resume took the watch over, it was dropped, or its file
      is gone; the line printed says which
  64  bad usage: no condition, an unknown or malformed id, an unknown codex run, a --pid that
      isn't watchable (not running, pid 1, a kernel thread, another user's), --max over 110,
      a second watch on a codex run that a watch already waits on, resuming an ended watch,
      or a run inside the sandbox
  70  internal error, or nothing could be decided (a finalize recorded no stop row, the codex
      run left the ledger): the watch stays open for a --resume; details in
      delegation-ledger.err
  75  still running at --max: re-arm with the command printed"""
WAIT_CONDITIONS = ("pid", "file", "log", "done", "fail", "stale", "codex")
CODEX_DELEGATE = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "codex-delegate")
FINALIZE_TIMEOUT_S = 300  # finalize checks a report and walks rollouts; the cap is 5 min off


def wait_condition(args):
    """The condition the options give, as the watch file stores it."""
    if args.codex is not None:
        if any(getattr(args, o) is not None for o in WAIT_CONDITIONS if o != "codex"):
            raise dc.WaitRefused("--codex takes no other condition")
        e = dc.find_codex(args.codex)
        if e is None:
            raise dc.WaitRefused(f"no codex run {args.codex!r} in the ledger ({dc.ledger_path()})")
        return {"codex": e["run_id"]}
    for opt in ("done", "fail", "stale"):
        if getattr(args, opt) is not None and args.log is None:
            raise dc.WaitRefused(f"--{opt} needs --log")
    if args.log is not None and args.done is None and args.fail is None and args.stale is None:
        raise dc.WaitRefused("--log needs --done, --fail or --stale")
    for opt in ("done", "fail"):
        pattern = getattr(args, opt)
        if pattern == "":
            raise dc.WaitRefused(f"--{opt} needs a pattern; an empty one matches every line")
        try:
            if pattern is not None:
                re.compile(pattern)
        except re.error as ex:
            raise dc.WaitRefused(f"--{opt} {pattern!r} is not a pattern ({ex})") from None
    if not (args.pid or args.file or args.done):
        raise dc.WaitRefused("give what to wait for: --pid, --file, --log with --done, or --codex")
    if args.stale is not None and not dc.is_positive(args.stale):
        raise dc.WaitRefused("--stale takes positive minutes")
    if args.pid and min(args.pid) <= 0:
        raise dc.WaitRefused("--pid takes a positive pid")
    cond = {}
    if args.pid:
        cond["pids"] = []
        for pid in dict.fromkeys(args.pid):
            why = dc.unwatchable(pid)
            if why:
                raise dc.WaitRefused(f"pid {pid} {why}; a pid echoed from a sandboxed command "
                                  "comes from another PID namespace")
            cond["pids"].append({"pid": pid, "start": dc.proc_start(pid),
                                 "comm": dc.proc_comm(pid)})
    if args.file:
        cond["file"] = os.path.abspath(args.file)
    if args.log:
        cond["log"] = os.path.abspath(args.log)
        cond.update((k, v) for k, v in (("done", args.done), ("fail", args.fail),
                                        ("stale_min", args.stale)) if v is not None)
    return cond


def existing_watch(wid):
    try:
        w = dc.read_watch(wid)
    except ValueError as ex:  # a bad id or a damaged file
        raise dc.WaitRefused(str(ex)) from None
    if w is None:
        raise dc.WaitRefused(f"no watch {wid!r}")
    return w


def same_watch(identity, cond):
    """The caller's unresolved watch on exactly this condition, or None. `identity` is the
    caller's claude_identity(). The watch is in its session, or one its Claude process left in
    a session that isn't live (dc.left_by_clear): an earlier session id, since a rerun after
    /clear may come before the guard's first stop adopts it, or "unknown", which matches by
    the process alone. A codex condition is left to the codex refusal (one watch per run), and
    a caller with neither a session nor a process has none."""
    me, session = identity
    if "codex" in cond or (session == "unknown" and me is None):
        return None
    live = dc.live_sessions() if me is not None else {}
    return next((w for w in dc.all_watches() if w.get("state") in dc.UNRESOLVED
                 and w.get("condition") == cond
                 and ((session != "unknown" and w.get("session_id") == session)
                      or dc.left_by_clear(w, me, live))), None)


def stop_row(run_id):
    """The folded codex entry when its latest row is a stop, else None."""
    e = dc.fold(dc.read_rows()).get(("codex", run_id)) or {}
    return e if e.get("event") == "stop" else None


class Waiter(dc.Waiter):
    """dc.Waiter polling a condition: `wait`'s loop, and the finalize a codex watch owes."""

    def run(self, max_min, new=None, taken=None):
        """Poll until the condition ends or max_min passes; the exit code. `taken` is printed
        once the watch is this waiter's, after its launch line."""
        deadline = time.monotonic() + max_min * 60
        w = self.take(new)
        # First, so a kill notice's output file names the watch (the guard folds by it).
        print(WAIT_LAUNCH.format(self.wid), flush=True)
        if taken:
            print(taken, flush=True)
        cursor = dc.log_cursor()
        while True:
            verdict, why = dc.watch_verdict(w, cursor)
            if verdict == "done" and "codex" in w["condition"]:
                verdict, why = self.codex_end(w["condition"]["codex"])
            if verdict:
                return self.record(verdict, why)
            left = deadline - time.monotonic()
            if left <= 0:
                print(dc.REARM.format(self.wid))
                return WAIT_AT_MAX
            time.sleep(min(self.poll, left))
            w = self.beat()

    def codex_end(self, run_id):
        """(verdict, why) once a codex run has ended: finalize it unless it has a stop row, then
        decide by the stop row's exit. (None, why) while another live waiter finalizes it."""
        e = stop_row(run_id)
        if e is None:
            if not self.claim_finalize():
                return None, f"codex run {run_id} is being finalized by another waiter"
            failure = self.finalize(run_id)
            e = stop_row(run_id)
            if e is None:
                raise dc.Undecidable(failure or f"codex-delegate finalize {run_id} exited 0 "
                                     "but recorded no stop row")
        return dc.codex_stopped(e)

    def claim_finalize(self):
        """Mark this waiter as the watch's finalizer, after checking under the lock that it
        still owns the watch; False when another live waiter is finalizing it."""
        claimed = False

        def claim(w):
            nonlocal claimed
            self.own(w)
            other = w.get("finalizing") or {}
            if other.get("pid") != self.me and dc.pid_alive(other.get("pid"),
                                                            other.get("start")):
                return
            w.update(finalizing={"pid": self.me, "start": self.start},
                     waiter_heartbeat=dc.now_iso())
            claimed = True
        dc.update_watch(self.wid, claim)
        return claimed

    def finalize(self, run_id):
        """Run the codex-delegate beside this script as `finalize <run_id>`, a fixed argv with
        its output passed on, heartbeating every poll while it runs: None when it exits 0, else
        why not. Taken over or dropped meanwhile, it lets finalize finish (the other waiter
        reads the stop row it writes), then steps aside. A beat that fails otherwise (a full
        disk, a damaged watch file) is logged and ends the heartbeat, but finalize is still
        waited on, so it never runs on unwatched beside a second one."""
        sys.stdout.flush()
        try:
            proc = subprocess.Popen([CODEX_DELEGATE, "finalize", run_id],
                                    stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        except OSError as ex:
            return f"codex-delegate finalize {run_id} didn't run ({ex})"
        deadline, aside, beating, rc = time.monotonic() + FINALIZE_TIMEOUT_S, None, True, None
        while True:
            try:
                rc = proc.wait(timeout=max(0.0, min(self.poll, deadline - time.monotonic())))
                break
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                pass
            if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                proc.kill()
                proc.wait()
                break
            if beating:
                try:
                    self.beat()
                except dc.StepAside as ex:
                    aside, beating = ex, False
                except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001  logged; finalize is still waited on
                    checks().log_error()
                    beating = False
        if aside is not None:
            raise aside
        if rc is None:
            return f"codex-delegate finalize {run_id} was stopped after {FINALIZE_TIMEOUT_S} s"
        return None if rc == 0 else f"codex-delegate finalize {run_id} exited {rc}"

    def record(self, verdict, why):
        """Record how the watch ended, print it, and return the exit code."""
        self.end(verdict)
        print(f"watch {self.wid} {verdict}: {why}")
        return WAIT_EXITS[verdict]


def drop_watch(wid):
    existing_watch(wid)  # a bad id, a damaged file or no such watch is bad usage
    prior = None

    def drop(w):
        # Decided under the lock, so a waiter that just ended the watch keeps its verdict, and
        # an ended watch isn't rewritten (update_watch skips a no-op), keeping its prune clock.
        nonlocal prior
        if not w:
            raise dc.WaitRefused(f"no watch {wid!r}")
        prior = w.get("state")
        if prior in dc.UNRESOLVED:
            w.update(state="dropped", ended=dc.now_iso())
    dc.update_watch(wid, drop)
    print(f"dropped watch {wid}" if prior in dc.UNRESOLVED else
          f"watch {wid} is already {prior}")
    return 0


def cmd_wait(args):
    if not dc.pids_visible():
        print(WAIT_SANDBOXED, file=sys.stderr)
        return WAIT_USAGE
    wid = args.resume
    try:
        if not (dc.is_positive(args.max) and dc.is_positive(args.poll)):
            raise dc.WaitRefused("--max and --poll take positive numbers")
        if args.max > dc.MAX_WAIT_MIN:
            raise dc.WaitRefused(f"--max must be at most {dc.MAX_WAIT_MIN}, under the Bash tool's "
                              "120-minute cap with room for a finalize")
        given = args.resume if args.resume is not None else args.drop
        if given is not None and (args.desc is not None or any(
                getattr(args, o) is not None for o in WAIT_CONDITIONS)):
            raise dc.WaitRefused("--resume and --drop take no condition or --desc")
        cond = wait_condition(args) if given is None else None
        dc.prune_watches()
        if args.drop is not None:
            return drop_watch(args.drop)
        identity = dc.claude_identity()  # one walk: the watch's process and session agree
        if args.resume is not None:
            existing_watch(wid)
            return Waiter(wid, args.poll, identity).run(args.max)
        same = same_watch(identity, cond)
        if same is not None:
            # A rerun of a killed waiter: carry on with its watch, which the guard names.
            return Waiter(same["id"], args.poll, identity).run(
                args.max, taken=f"watch {same['id']} already waits on this; taking it over")
        wid = dc.new_watch_id()
        if identity[0] is None:  # with a process, its guard adopts even an "unknown" session
            print("no Claude Code session: the watch guard won't see this watch",
                  file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        return Waiter(wid, args.poll, identity).run(args.max, new={
            "id": wid, "session_id": identity[1], "condition": cond,
            "description": args.desc or dc.condition_text(cond), "created": dc.now_iso()})
    except dc.WaitRefused as ex:
        print(f"wait: {ex}", file=sys.stderr)
        return WAIT_USAGE
    except dc.StepAside as ex:
        print(ex)
        return WAIT_ASIDE
    except dc.Undecidable as ex:
        checks().log_error(f"wait {wid}: {ex}; the watch stays open")
        print(f"wait: {ex}; watch {wid} stays open, so `delegation-ledger wait --resume {wid}` "
              "tries again", file=sys.stderr)
        return WAIT_ERROR
    except Exception as ex:  # noqa: BLE001  logged, and the watch stays for a resume
        checks().log_error()
        print(f"wait: {type(ex).__name__}: {ex} (traceback in "
              f"{os.path.join(dc.state_dir(), 'delegation-ledger.err')})", file=sys.stderr)
        return WAIT_ERROR


class Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):
    """An ArgumentParser whose usage errors exit `usage_code`: argparse's 2, unless a subcommand
    sets its own (wait's 2 means a stale log, so its bad usage is WAIT_USAGE)."""
    usage_code = 2

    def error(self, message):
        self.print_usage(sys.stderr)
        self.exit(self.usage_code, f"{self.prog}: error: {message}\n")


def main(argv=None):
    ap = Parser(prog="delegation-ledger", description=__doc__.split("\n")[0])
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)  # its parsers are Parsers too
    sub.add_parser("hook").set_defaults(fn=cmd_hook)
    o = sub.add_parser("open")
    o.add_argument("--hours", type=float, default=48)
    o.set_defaults(fn=cmd_open)
    w = sub.add_parser("watch")
    w.add_argument("--summary", action="store_true",
                   help="one token for the tmux status bar, like `2▶ 1⚠`; empty when none")
    w.set_defaults(fn=cmd_watch)
    t = sub.add_parser("tail")
    t.add_argument("-n", type=int, default=20)
    t.set_defaults(fn=cmd_tail)
    a = sub.add_parser("audit")
    a.add_argument("--hours", type=float, default=None,
                   help="the window: 168 by default, 720 with --monthly")
    a.add_argument("--monthly", action="store_true",
                   help="a month's window, plus the usage sections for retuning")
    a.add_argument("--unshown", action="store_true", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)  # due's daily run
    a.set_defaults(fn=cmd_audit)
    x = sub.add_parser("exclude")
    x.add_argument("--id", help="an agent id (or codex run id)")
    x.add_argument("--session", help="a session id")
    x.add_argument("--name", help="a name, as a teammate or a named-spawn denial records it")
    x.add_argument("--why", required=True, help="the reason audit --monthly prints, like probe")
    x.set_defaults(fn=cmd_exclude)
    s = sub.add_parser("sandbox-denials")
    s.add_argument("--days", type=float, default=7)
    s.set_defaults(fn=cmd_sandbox_denials)
    c = sub.add_parser("canary")
    c.add_argument("--quick", action="store_true",
                   help="only the quick tier: no model calls, runs inside the sandbox")
    c.add_argument("--accept-fewer", action="store_true",
                   help="go green although the harness ran fewer checks than the last green run")
    c.set_defaults(fn=cmd_canary)
    d = sub.add_parser("due")
    d.add_argument("--hook", action="store_true", help="the SessionStart body (fails open)")
    d.add_argument("--background", nargs="*", choices=("quick", "audit"), help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    d.set_defaults(fn=cmd_due)
    wt = sub.add_parser("wait", epilog=WAIT_EXIT_HELP,
                        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    wt.usage_code = WAIT_USAGE
    wt.add_argument("--pid", type=int, action="append",
                    help="a pid running now; done when it has exited (repeat it to wait for "
                         "all)")
    wt.add_argument("--file", help="done when this path exists")
    wt.add_argument("--log", help="a log to watch, with --done, --fail and --stale")
    wt.add_argument("--done", metavar="RE", help="done once a --log line matches")
    wt.add_argument("--fail", metavar="RE", help="failed (exit 1) once a --log line matches")
    wt.add_argument("--stale", type=float, metavar="MIN",
                    help="stale (exit 2) once --log hasn't changed for MIN minutes")
    wt.add_argument("--codex", metavar="RUN_ID",
                    help="wait for the codex run to end, finalize it unless it has a stop "
                         "row, and exit by the stop row's exit")
    wt.add_argument("--desc", help="what the watch is for (default: its condition)")
    wt.add_argument("--max", type=float, default=dc.MAX_WAIT_MIN, metavar="MIN",
                    help=f"exit 75 with the re-arm command after this long (default and most: "
                         f"{dc.MAX_WAIT_MIN})")
    wt.add_argument("--poll", type=float, default=dc.WAIT_POLL_S, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    again = wt.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    again.add_argument("--resume", metavar="ID", help="take over this watch and wait on")
    again.add_argument("--drop", metavar="ID", help="stop watching it")
    wt.set_defaults(fn=cmd_wait)
    args, extra = ap.parse_known_args(argv)
    if extra:  # argparse would report these from the top parser; the subcommand's code applies
        sub.choices[args.cmd].error(f"unrecognized arguments: {' '.join(extra)}")
    return args.fn(args)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
